<title>USA: Kennecott Copper readied in case of strike.</title>
<headline>Kennecott Copper readied in case of strike.</headline>
<dateline>SALT LAKE CITY 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kennecott Corp said on Tuesday it would run its Utah Copper mining and smelting operation with management employees if union mine workers walk off the job.</p>
<p>Negotiations with national representatives of the United Steelworkers of America Union which represents 85 percent of the hourly workers at the Utah copper division, reopened on Tuesday, Tracey Stevenson, senior vice president, finance and control for Kennecott said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are prepared to keep operations going,&quot; Stevenson said.</p>
</text>
